SYDO Implementations
====================

This directory contains the reference and optimized NGCC submission packages
for all SYDO signature instances.


Layout
------

```text
Implementations/
  README
  NOTICE
  Reference_Implementation/
    sydo_160s/
    sydo_160f/
    sydo_256s/
    sydo_256f/
    sydo_512s/
    sydo_512f/
  Optimized_Implementation/
    sydo_160s/
    sydo_160f/
    sydo_256s/
    sydo_256f/
    sydo_512s/
    sydo_512f/
```

Every `sydo_*` instance directory has the same local structure:

```text
Makefile                  build file for this instance
SIG_AlgorithmInstance.c   NGCC signature API wrapper
SIG_AlgorithmInstance.h   NGCC signature API header
src/                      algorithm implementation
lib/                      auxfunc/drng and bundled primitives
test/                     KAT and benchmark drivers
```


Instances
---------

| Instance | Reference package | Optimized package |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `sydo_160s` | `Reference_Implementation/sydo_160s` | `Optimized_Implementation/sydo_160s` |
| `sydo_160f` | `Reference_Implementation/sydo_160f` | `Optimized_Implementation/sydo_160f` |
| `sydo_256s` | `Reference_Implementation/sydo_256s` | `Optimized_Implementation/sydo_256s` |
| `sydo_256f` | `Reference_Implementation/sydo_256f` | `Optimized_Implementation/sydo_256f` |
| `sydo_512s` | `Reference_Implementation/sydo_512s` | `Optimized_Implementation/sydo_512s` |
| `sydo_512f` | `Reference_Implementation/sydo_512f` | `Optimized_Implementation/sydo_512f` |


Build Requirements
------------------

| Package | Requirements |
| --- | --- |
| Reference | POSIX `make`; ISO C compiler with C11 support, such as GCC or Clang |
| Optimized | POSIX `make`; GCC/G++ with C23 and C++23 support; x86-64 CPU with AVX2, AES-NI, PCLMULQDQ, and SSSE3 |

`taskset` from util-linux is recommended on Linux for single-core benchmarks.


Build, Benchmark, And KAT
------------------------

Reference example:

```sh
cd Reference_Implementation/sydo_160s
make clean
make CC=gcc
taskset -c 0 ./bench
./kat_sig
```

Optimized example:

```sh
cd Optimized_Implementation/sydo_160s
make clean
make CC=gcc CXX=g++
taskset -c 0 ./bench
./kat_sig
```

Use the same idle CPU core for all benchmark runs when comparing instances.
Each `kat_sig` run writes `output/KAT_SIG_<AlgorithmInstance>.txt`.


Submitted Test Vectors
----------------------

```text
../Test_Vectors/KAT_SIG_sydo_160s.txt
../Test_Vectors/KAT_SIG_sydo_160f.txt
../Test_Vectors/KAT_SIG_sydo_256s.txt
../Test_Vectors/KAT_SIG_sydo_256f.txt
../Test_Vectors/KAT_SIG_sydo_512s.txt
../Test_Vectors/KAT_SIG_sydo_512f.txt
```


Primitive Interfaces
--------------------

- Transcript/hash XOF calls use the NGCC auxiliary `lib/auxfunc.c` `pseudoXOF`.
- Randomness uses `lib/drng.c`.
- For non-512-bit parameter sets, GGM PRG and leaf commitments use Rijndael,
  and expand-h PRG uses AES.
- For 512-bit parameter sets, the special-case primitive paths use the
  BLAKE2s-derived 512-bit block-cipher primitive.
